# HR-002: Paid Time Off (PTO) Policy

**MedSync Health**
**Document ID:** HR-002
**Version:** 1.0
**Effective Date:** January 1, 2026
**Owner:** HR & People Department (Rachel Williams, CHRO)

---

## 1. Policy Statement and Purpose

The Paid Time Off (PTO) policy at MedSync Health is designed to provide employees with paid time away from work for rest, relaxation, personal appointments, and minor illness. We believe that taking regular time off is essential for maintaining employee well-being, productivity, and preventing burnout, supporting our global workforce of **1,200 employees** across our main offices in **Boston, MA, London, UK, Berlin, Germany, and Singapore**.

This policy is governed by the principles outlined in the general employee handbook. **See HR-001 for general policies** regarding employment standards, code of conduct, and disciplinary procedures.

## 2. Eligibility and Accrual

### 2.1 Eligibility

All regular full-time employees of MedSync Health are eligible to accrue and use PTO from their date of hire. Part-time employees accrue PTO on a pro-rata basis based on their scheduled hours. Contractors and temporary staff are not eligible for PTO under this policy.

### 2.2 PTO Accrual Rates

PTO is accrued on a bi-weekly basis. The annual allotment is tiered based on the employee's job level, recognizing the increasing demands and responsibilities at higher organizational tiers.

| Job Level | Annual PTO Allotment (Days) | Accrual Rate (Days per Bi-Weekly Pay Period) |
|:----------|:----------------------------|:---------------------------------------------|
| **IC** (Individual Contributor) | 20 | 0.769 |
| **Manager** | 22 | 0.846 |
| **Director** | 25 | 0.961 |
| **VP** (Vice President) | 30 | 1.154 |

*Note: The accrual rate is calculated based on 26 bi-weekly pay periods per year.*

## 3. Usage and Approval Process

### 3.1 Requesting PTO

Employees must submit PTO requests through the designated HR information system (HRIS). Requests should be submitted as far in advance as possible to allow for proper departmental planning.

### 3.2 Approval

All PTO requests require approval from the employee's direct manager. Managers will review requests based on departmental staffing needs and operational requirements. Requests for three (3) or more consecutive days of PTO should be submitted at least four (4) weeks in advance.

### 3.3 Maximum Usage

Employees are encouraged to use their accrued PTO throughout the year. Employees may not take more than ten (10) consecutive working days of PTO without prior approval from both their direct manager and the Head of HR & People.

## 4. Carryover and Payout

### 4.1 PTO Carryover

To ensure employees take necessary time off, MedSync Health enforces a PTO carryover limit. Employees may carry over a maximum of **five (5) days** of unused PTO into the next calendar year. Any accrued PTO balance exceeding this limit on December 31st will be forfeited.

### 4.2 PTO Payout (Termination)

Upon separation from MedSync Health, whether voluntary or involuntary, employees will be paid for any accrued, unused PTO balance in accordance with applicable state and local laws for their respective location (Boston, London, Berlin, or Singapore). PTO is not paid out in lieu of taking time off during employment.

